# CYCLE 1 — Foundation + injections

## Generator

Design intent: a 4.2 m3/s axial-flow fen-polder land-drain where three
correct agents each read a drain-mean loop because a peat slip on intake
screen 3 partitions local screen dP from still-well mean, shaft speed,
and penstock stroke. The naive playbook raises pump speed into a packed
screen. The gate must MODIFY on a numeric pump floor, not by killing an
agent. sim_or_real=designed. Reward heads are
task_progress/safety/efficiency/coherence/exploration.

Cycle-1 base arc (pre-critic): state at Reedholt PS-4, 1.42 m AOD,
LVL 1.42 m, PMP 48.0 Hz, WIR 820 mm, proposed RAISE-PUMP
54.0 Hz, safety MODIFY to PUMP-HOLD, executed hold without the
flush-probe numbers fully specified, outcome "slip found, polder saved"
(this last claim is the defect the later cycles will refuse to keep).
Sixteen spikes, five ticks, raster/gate_snn present but the scar is a
single edge.

